    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d663">

                <pb facs="0811" n="797" xml:id="pg797"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.20 Defense/3560</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Venezuela</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Flack</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 4504</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Caracas</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-06-12">June 12, 1943</date>.<lb/>[Received June
                        22.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Confirming my telegram No. 522 of June 7, 6
                        p.m.,<anchor n="12" xml:id="d663-f1"/> I have the honor to enclose a copy of
                    my Note No. 1341 of June 3, 1943 to the Foreign Minister and a copy of the
                    Minister’s note No. 1528 of June 10, 1943 in reply.<anchor n="13"
                        xml:id="d663-f2"/> Oral approval of the request was communicated to me on
                    June 7, as previously reported by telegram.<anchor n="14" xml:id="d663-f3"/></p>
                <p>The description of the proposed extension of the danger areas was supplied to me
                    by the Naval Attaché and incorporated in my note of June 3, 1943, which I handed
                    personally to the Foreign Minister on the morning of June 4, 1943.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Joseph Flack</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d663-f1" n="12" xml:id="d663-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d663-f2" n="13" xml:id="d663-f2-content">
                <p>Neither printed; these notes indicated the desire of the United States Navy to
                    extend the mine fields in the Gulf of Paria and the Venezuelan acquiescence.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d663-f3" n="14" xml:id="d663-f3-content">
                <p>No. 522, June 7, 1943, not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
